    "importer": {
      "answer": "Implemented only `import_rows` in `importer.py`; all 4 public tests now pass.\n\n## Evidence\n- Pre-edit actual run: `test_money` ok, `test_negative_rounding` ok, `test_dedup` FAIL (`2 != 1`), `test_utc` FAIL (`{'2026-10-12': 200} != {'2026-10-11': 200}`).\n- Post-edit actual run: **exit=0, Ran 4 tests, OK** — all four pass.\n\n## What `import_rows` now does (per docs/api.txt)\n- Accepts each row's `id`, `timestamp`, `amount`, optional `revision` (default 0).\n- `id`: stripped and NFC-normalized, never lowercased; empty → `ValueError`.\n- `timestamp`: ISO8601 via `datetime.fromisoformat`, accepting a trailing `Z`; aware timestamps converted to UTC before taking the date, naive treated as UTC; invalid → `ValueError`.\n- `amount`: delegated to the unchanged `parse_amount`.\n- `revision`: must be a non-negative `int` (bools rejected) else `ValueError`.\n- Dedup by normalized id, keeping the highest revision; at equal revision the **last** input wins (in-place replace preserves first-seen ordering).\n- No input mutation (new dicts only) and no module-global state — dedup state is local per call.\n\n`parser.py` was left byte-for-byte unchanged (`test_money`/`test_negative_rounding` still pass), and `report.py` was not edited — its `daily_totals` now works via the fixed `import_rows`, while `running_balance`/`report_metadata` remain report-phase work and were untouched.\n\nStopping here; report work is not authorized in this phase.",
