    "report": {
      "answer": "Implemented `report.py` under the current v2 contract; all 4 public tests pass.\n\n## Evidence\n- Pre-edit actual run: **exit=1**, `test_balance` ERROR (`NotImplementedError: balance implementation missing`), `test_live_metadata` FAIL (`{'api_revision': 'legacy-api'} != {'api_revision': 'public-new-revision'}`); `test_money`, `test_utc` ok.\n- Post-edit actual run: **exit=0, Ran 4 tests, OK** — all four pass.\n\n## What changed (only `report.py`)\n- `daily_totals(rows)`: now calls the module-level `importer.import_rows(rows)` (looked up at call time) to dedupe — highest revision, ties last — and sums integer cents per UTC day into a fresh dict. No shared state, no input mutation.\n- `running_balance(rows, opening_cents=0)`: validates `opening_cents` (rejects `bool` and non-`int` with `ValueError`), then walks `daily_totals(rows)` in day-ascending order accumulating the running total. Returns new dicts with exact keys `day` and `balance_cents`; empty rows returns `[]`.\n- `report_metadata()`: returns `{\"api_revision\": importer.API_REVISION}`, reading the live attribute each call rather than a frozen literal (verified by `test_live_metadata`, which temporarily rebinds `importer.API_REVISION`).\n\n`parser.py` and `importer.py` were not modified — confirmed by `test_money`/`test_utc` still passing and untouched file contents. No publishing or deployment performed.",
